I'd like to suggest that we put the name of the user group to a vote at the
first meeting.

I think we can do better than SELUG -- it is too likely to be pronounced
"slug" which suggests that the operating system is slow and unresponsive.

As an alternative, I'd like to suggest "Capital Area Security Enhanced
Linux" user group--pronounced "castle" user group--which suggests a fortress
or stronghold designed to keep out intruders.

I think that forming an association between SE Linux and a castle would do
more to aid our common goal of promoting SE Linux.  In any case, I think we
can do better.

- Michael Pender




